<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="878d8179-6b7a-5986-8253-610222585b96" activityNameId="d162115f-b5f1-55e5-9fca-f2b183b8da8e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, concrete, 5% water, to construction waste landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, concrete, 5% water, to construction waste landfill
This dataset represents the activity of waste disposal of waste concrete in a construction waste landfill. Recommended use of this dataset: For waste concrete material going to landfill. Can be used for /reinforced/ concrete or /not reinforced/ concrete. For the former, the mass without the reinforcement steel must be inventoried with this dataset, and the reinforcement steel additionally and separately with a steel to construction waste landfill dataset.Inventoried waste consists of fraction: 100% Concrete; . Waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O 50000; O 517270; H 22896; C 3256.5; S 1365.5; N 14.727; P 431.64; B 8.6369; Cl 118.02; Br 0.6602; F 453.65; I 0.16621; Ag 0.039212; As 3.2798; Ba 388.34; Cd 0.20757; Co 5.6914; Cr 22.54; Cu 17.611; Hg 0.032791; Mn 364.95; Mo 0.914; Ni 14.179; Pb 22.105; Sb 0.46028; Se 3.3533; Sn 2.8855; V 32.846; Zn 63.941; Be 2.1999; Sc 9.2689; Sr 257.11; Ti 3458.5; Tl 0.4283; W 1.0344; Si 234790; Fe 12170; Ca 89232; Al 33885; K 15417; Mg 3576.2; Na 10442. Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%.;; UUID: 19c2ddb6-68b0-4d8a-97e0-a8aa9a4d8ca0
Waste-specific short-term emissions via landfill leachate. Waste-specific long-term emissions from landfill.  Land transformation and occupation. Waste placement and compaction. Landfill construction materials, sewer pipe for leachate, and access road.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: This is an inventory for a construction waste landfill (mostly mineral C&amp;D waste, VVEA type B). Ultimate average landfill height is 11 meters. Operation phase duration is 15 years.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on average mineral building waste composition and observed average leachate concentrations from various literature sources. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics and hydrology. Based on waste composition and climate data the end of carbonate phase of this landfill is estimated to be reached beyond 60'000 years. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. *Mean* long-term emissions are the emissions until 60'000 years after waste placement. *Maximal* (upper bound) long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material, depicting possible mechanical landfill failures and/or natural erosion not heeded in the mean value. Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_19c2ddb6-68b0-4d8a-97e0-a8aa9a4d8ca0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
